35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, the call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, but the shared round lost a third of visits. We need robust infrastructure, not just good intentions.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, the infrastructure is already saturated. Rooms book out by mid-morning, and the shuttle misses most villages. We cannot absorb more without seizing up.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the minutes confirm my fear: the joint clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. We are building on sand again.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, the joint clinic failure is a warning. But look at the staffing: physios are leaving, yet midwives have slack. We must match the program to who is actually available.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@All, the ledger is down a quarter, and off-site care earns nothing. We must choose a program that bills on-site to sustain itself.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, on-site billing is vital, but the trial proved home visits work. We need a model that captures that value without losing the patients.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, on-site billing is a trap. The booking system only records named slots. If we can’t log the work, we can’t bill it, regardless of location.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the data agreements took fourteen months. Any program relying on outside surgeries is dead on arrival. We need self-contained structures.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, fourteen months is too long. But @Servas, the midwifery slack is real. We have capacity there, unlike the therapy team.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, the midwifery slack is a gift. We must use it wisely. A program that fits our current strength is the only one that will truly endure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, midwifery slack is a resource, not a guarantee. @Servas, if the budget is down, we must prioritize programs with proven, measurable outcomes to justify the spend.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, measurable outcomes are useless if the system cannot process them. If the booking screens are full, the data simply vanishes.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, fourteen months is a death sentence. Any program needing outside data is structurally doomed. We need self-contained units, not fragile partnerships.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But @Servas, the midwifery slack is our only real capacity. We must build on what we have, not what we wish we had.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, I agree. We must build on solid ground. A program using existing midwifery strength avoids the structural rot Benjamin fears.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, I agree. The trial proved home visits work, but the shared round failed. We need a self-contained model that bills on-site to survive the budget cut.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, self-contained is necessary, but not sufficient. If the booking system cannot log the work, it vanishes from the records. We need a model that fits the existing slots.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. If it isn’t a named slot, it doesn’t exist. We need a program that fits the current architecture, not one that demands a rebuild.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree. If it isn’t logged, it doesn’t exist. But @Servas, the midwifery slack is our only real capacity. We must build on what we have, not what we wish we had.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@All, the evidence points to one path. We must choose the program that fits our current strength and bills on-site. Let us vote.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
